 created planning step, not `to_messages`. Fine.\\n\\nAlso check `replay` in memory.py — uses `step.facts` which doesn't exist anymore (dataclass has plan only). That's a pre-existing bug, not related.\\n\\nAlso, are there other tests that count messages, e.g., tests asserting write_memory_to_messages content for planning? Let me grep test_agents for \\\"to_messages\\\" and \\\"write_memory_to_messages\\\" counts related to planning.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"I now have the full picture. The behavior the user wants maps to how the agent's conversation history is built from memory: `PlanningStep.to_messages()` converts a plan into conversation messages — it should append a single `USER` message after the plan, but only in full (non-summary) mode. Let me check tests that might be affected by message counts."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8e8076460b75b7c","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"grep -rn \"write_memory_to_messages\\|to_messages\" /testbed/tests/test_agents.py | head -20; grep -rn \"write_memory_to_messages\" /testbed/src/smolagents/agents.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"harbor-endpoint","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":5503,"output":1446,"cacheRead":9216,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1319,"totalTokens":16165,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788469979696,"responseId":"gen-1788469979-mrnxspsI3PdJvqM3Dx6G","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-b8e8076460b75b7c","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"543:        assert \"Error raised in check\" in str(agent.write_memory_to_messages())\n907:        agent.write_memory_to_messages = MagicMock(return_value=[{\"content\": \"Test summary\"}])\n430:            memory_messages = self.write_memory_to_messages(summary_mode=True)\n483:    def write_memory_to_messages(\n546:        messages += self.write_memor