hen the full conversation is being displayed (not in summary mode)\\\" maps exactly to `to_messages(summary_mode=False)` vs `summary_mode=True`. The \\\"display\\\" here is about how the conversation history is presented to the model. The memory's PlanningStep.to_messages is the mechanism.\\n\\nAlso note \\\"exactly once after each plan\\\" — each PlanningStep produces exactly one such message. This rules out e.g. adding it in `write_memory_to_messages` in a way that duplicates, or adding it both in gradio UI and memory.\\n\\nThe core fix: modify `PlanningStep.to_messages` in memory.py. This makes the user message appear in the conversation whenever the plan is included (not summary mode), exactly once per planning step.\\n\\nShould I also update gradio_ui? Let me check the upstream gradio_ui at master:\\n\\n```python\\n    elif isinstance(step_log, PlanningStep):\\n        yield gr.ChatMessage(role=\\\"assistant\\\", content=\\\"**Planning step**\\\")\\n        yield gr.ChatMessage(role=\\\"assistant\\\", content=step_log.plan)\\n        yield gr.ChatMessage(role=\\\"assistant\\\", content=get_step_footnote_content(step_log, \\\"Planning step\\\"))\\n        yield gr.ChatMessage(role=\\\"assistant\\\", content=\\\"-----\\\", metadata={\\\"status\\\": \\\"done\\\"})\\n```\\n\\nI believe upstream gradio_ui.py doesn't yield the user message — the display in the UI stays assistant-only. The \\\"user-style message\\\" is in the memory for the model. Given the user's description \\\"prevent the AI from simply continuing to elaborate on the plan instead of moving forward with action\\\" — this is about the model's context, not the visual UI. So the memory change is the right one.\\n\\nNow let me also check `test_agents.py::test_planning_step` to ensure it doesn't break — it checks `model_input_messages` of the created planning step, not `to_messages`. Fine.\\n\\nAlso check `replay` in memory.py — uses `step.facts` which doesn't exist anymore (dataclass has plan only). Tha