write_memory_to_messages(summary_mode=True)\n\nplan_texts = [m for m in full if \"plan of action\" in str(m[\"content\"])]\nfollowups = [m for m in full if m[\"role\"] == MessageRole.USER and \"Now go on and execute this plan.\" in str(m[\"content\"])]\nprint(\"full-mode messages:\", len(full))\nprint(\"plan messages:\", len(plan_texts), \"| follow-up user messages:\", len(followups))\nprint(\"follow-up message:\", followups[0])\nprint(\"summary-mode messages:\", len(summary))\nassert len(followups) == 1\nassert summary == []\nprint(\"OK: exactly one follow-up in full mode, none in summary mode\")\nEOF","timeout":300}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"harbor-endpoint","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":18111,"output":445,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":59,"totalTokens":18556,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788470132980,"responseId":"gen-1788470133-1h8xNmXCYCMJD1lqvYdW","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-90929cc2a703179c","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"full-mode messages: 3\nplan messages: 1 | follow-up user messages: 1\nfollow-up message: {'role': <MessageRole.USER: 'user'>, 'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'Now go on and execute this plan.'}]}\nsummary-mode messages: 0\nOK: exactly one follow-up in full mode, none in summary mode\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788470147603},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The end-to-end check confirms:\n1. Full conversation mode: plan (assistant) followed by exactly one user message \"Now go on and execute this plan.\"\n2. Summary mode: nothing (no plan, no follow-up).\n\nLet me view the final diff to summarize.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"The end-to-end check confirms:\\n1. Full conversation mode: plan (assistant) followed by exactly one user message \\\"Now go on and execute this plan.\\\"\\n2. Summary mode: nothing (no plan, no follow-up).\\n\\nLet me view the final diff to summarize.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"Everything works as required. Here's a summary of the change:\n\n## Change\n\n**`src/smolagents/memory.py`** — `PlanningStep.to_messages()` (the single choke point through which every plan — initial or updated — is turned into conversation history):\n\n```python\ndef to_messages(self, summary_mode: bool, **kwargs) -> List[Message]:\n    if summary_mode:\n        return []\n    return [\n        Message(role=MessageRole.ASSISTANT, content=[{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": self.plan.strip()}]),\n        Message(role=MessageRole.USER, content=[{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Now go on and execute this plan.\"}]),\n    ]\n```\n\n**`tests/test_memory.py`** — updated `test_planning_step_to_messages` to assert the new two-message structure (assistant plan → user follow-up), and added `test_planning_step_to_messages_summary_mode` asserting an empty result in summary mode.\n\n## Why this satisfies each requirement\n\n- **Automatic & consistent**: Every planning step flows through `PlanningStep.to_messages()` when the agent builds its conversation (via `write_memory_to_messages`), so the instruction is attached to *every* plan with no per-agent configuration.\n- **User-style message**: It's a `MessageRole.USER` message, creating the natural handoff that tells the model to stop planning and start acting.\n- **Exactly once per plan**: One follow-up message is emitted per `PlanningStep`, immediately after the plan content — verified in the end-to-end check (`follow-up user messages: 1`).\n- **Full conversation only**: In summary mode (`summary_mode=True`), `to_messages` returns `[]`, so neither the plan nor the follow-up appears — matching how planning messages were already excluded from summary context.\n\nAll 64 tests in `test_agents.py` + `test_memory.py` pass."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"harbor-endpoint","mod